omment-5273448487","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122031","id":5273448487,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOlJwJw","user":{"login":"Synzorasize","id":60207816,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMjA3ODE2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60207816?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize","html_url":"https://github.com/Synzorasize","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-12T22:20:31Z","updated_at":"2026-08-12T22:20:31Z","body":"It seems like it crashes on the third test case, but how do we know what that test case is? It could also be a bug with the test runner, but I'd like to see that test first to see if excluding it might make it segfault on something else. (I'm also unsure of what `optimize=\"none\"` or `optimize=\"debug\"` does exactly)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5273448487/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5302800937","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122031#issuecomment-5302800937","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122031","id":5302800937,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPBJSKQ","user":{"login":"leandro-benedet-garcia","id":291051,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTA1MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/291051?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandro-benedet-garcia","html_url":"https://github.com/leandro-benedet-garcia","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandro-benedet-garcia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandro-benedet-garcia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandro-benedet-garcia/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandro-benedet-garcia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandro-benedet-garcia/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandro-benedet-garcia/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandro-benedet-garcia/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandro-benedet-garcia/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandro-benedet-garcia/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-15T15:00:59Z","updated_at":"2026-08-15T17:33:16Z","body":"While trying to compile with this `custom.py` the dev symbols outright never gets generated:\n```python\ncompiledb = \"yes\"\nstrict_checks = \"yes\"\nuse_llvm = \"yes\"\nlinker = \"mold\"\ndev_mode=\"yes\"\noptimize = \"none\"\ndebug_symbols = \"yes\"\nseparate_debug_symbols = \"yes\"\n```\n\nEven though I explicitly told it to.\nSo I enabled `dev_build` and compiled the engine, the bug didn't happen.\n\nSo I went into the scons file, commented this line:\n`env.Append(CPPDEFINES=[\"DEV_ENABLED\"])`\n\nAnd then the bug did happen. And the debug symbols did generate. With the debug symbols I spun up LLDB. I don't think this was supposed to happen:\n\n<img width=\"1372\" height=\"1164\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f8614f35-56d9-4624-a895-e4f0d382aa8d\" />\n\nGoing trough the call stack until before the recursion (took me a bit to scroll everything), we get to here.\n\n<img width=\"1374\" height=\"924\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9f5633a1-8d5f-4c60-8915-902dbb5c5ea0\" />\n\nHere's the line that triggers the recursion:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/00932449c9f372b30301d8b5fdc1be70ec12b5c0/modules/gdscript/tests/gdscript_test_runner.cpp#L684\n\nHere's the complete callstack\n[callstack.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/31103079/callstack.log)\n\nUnless I am doing something wrong? But if I did, it shouldn't crash anyway. as far as I know.\n\nThis bug might be related to this issue: \n#104699\n\nEDIT:\nThe recursion is actually intended. I checked the function name with the debugger. It is `is_prime`\n\nSearching the code base, there's only one function named `is_prime`, it is under `modules/gdscript/tests/scripts/runtime/features/recursion.gd`\n\nIf you lower the number of the prime to something in the range of, for example `1931`, the crash never happens.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5302800937/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]